<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐσταθ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>, 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐϋστ</span>-, as always in <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵσταμαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>well-based, well-built</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τοῖχον ἐϋσταθέος μεγάροιο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					18.374
				</span></i>
			, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντὸς ἐϋσταθέος μεγάρου,
				ἐκτὸς ἐϋ. θαλάμου</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				20.258
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				23.178
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>steadfast, tranquil</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Democr.
					191
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.44a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ -έστεροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdn.
					2.6.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνώμη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SA</u>
					1.10
				</span></i>
			; -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έστεροι γνώμῃ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				2.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τῆς εὐσταθοῦς τῶν θεῶν
				διαγωγῆς</span> dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>D.</u>
				3t
			</span></i>it. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of the
			body, <i>sound, healthy</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαρκὸς εὐσταθὲς κατάστημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					68
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Metrod.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; of persons, <i>healthy, sound</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
			</span></i>
			
				Med.
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
			</span></i>inc.<i><span class="en">
				7.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. νοῦσοι</span>
			<i>easily cured, not serious</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				3.8
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καῦσοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Epid.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of weather,
				<i>steady, settled, calm</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέρος</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				3.15
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζέφυρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.821
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> generally,
				<i>steady, quiet</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					p.53A.
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁρμονία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Dem.</u>
					36
				</span></i>
			; in political sense, <i>firmly established</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοναρχία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Hom.</u>
					p.31
				</span></i>
			 O. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῶς, ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.40
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				7.182
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Asp.
				<u>in EN</u>
				115.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατοπεδεῦσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>Hisp.</u>
					25
				</span></i>
			, al.: 
				Sup.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έστατα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>BC</u>
				2.115
			</span></i>; 
				Aeol.
			 -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(2).243
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Mytilene</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
